.1)TF-IDF: It helps search systems identify documents containing terms that are particularly informative.

FUTMxStore example: The term "thermodynamics" may receive a high weight in a document about thermodynamics if it is frequent there but uncommon across the wider collection of academic materials.

2.)Cosine similarity measures the cosine of the angle between two vectors, providing a measure of how closely aligned their directions are. In information retrieval, it can be used to score the similarity between a query vector and document vectors, helping rank candidate documents.
